## psc/parse/stmt/core.pengu — statements, bloques y control de flujo.
##
## Cubre `stmt` y `block` de la gramática. Los constructos que pueden usarse
## como valor (`if`, `when`, `for`, `while`) también se implementan aquí; el
## hook `PsHooks.value` los reutiliza desde `stmt/values.pengu`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye nodos en el AST; no asigna strings salvo diagnósticos.

import psc.span as pspan
import psc.source as psource
import psc.token as pstoken

import psc.ast.kind as pskind
import psc.ast.node as psast
import psc.parse.state as psstate
import psc.parse.diagnostics as pdiag
import psc.parse.types as ptypes
import psc.parse.expr.ops as pexpr
import psc.parse.expr.atoms as patoms

insignia psc_parse_stmt_

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bloques y listas de statements
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Parsea el cuerpo de un bloque y añade sus `stmt` al nodo en construcción.
##
## ## Retorno
## Número de statements parseados.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(statements del bloque).
weave pstmt_parse_block_members with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var count as int is 0
    if calling ps_check with p, TokNewline:
        var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokIndent, "indent"
        var more as bool is true
        while more:
            calling ps_skip_newlines with p
            if (calling ps_check with p, TokDedent) or (calling ps_check with p, TokEof):
                set more is false
            else:
                var before as int is p->pos
                var st as int is calling pstmt_parse_stmt with p
                calling ps_add_child with p, st
                set count is count + 1
                calling pstmt_check_multiple with p
                if p->pos == before:
                    var forced as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        if count == 0:
            calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseEmptyBlock, ""
        if calling ps_check with p, TokDedent:
            var ignored4 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        else:
            calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedDedent, ""
    else:
        var simple as int is calling pstmt_parse_simple_stmt with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, simple
        calling ps_finish_statement with p
        set count is 1
    return count

## Parsea `":"` + bloque.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `block` con `stmt` hijos.
weave pstmt_parse_block with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokColon, "':'"
    if not (calling ps_enter_block with p):
        var off as int is calling ps_current_start with p
        return calling ps_error_node with p, off, off
    defer calling ps_leave_block with p
    return calling pstmt_parse_block_body with p

## Parsea `":"` + bloque añadiendo los `stmt` directamente al nodo actual.
##
## Se usa en `weave`, `test`, `with_stmt`, `do:`, `with:` y `or:`.
##
## ## Memoria
## No crea nodo `block`; añade los `stmt` al nodo en construcción.
weave pstmt_parse_block_into with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokColon, "':'"
    if not (calling ps_enter_block with p):
        return
    defer calling ps_leave_block with p
    var ignored2 as int is calling pstmt_parse_block_members with p

## Parsea el cuerpo de un bloque cuando el `:` ya se consumió.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `block` con `stmt` hijos.
weave pstmt_parse_block_body with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    var ignored as int is calling pstmt_parse_block_members with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdBlock, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Parsea el cuerpo de un bloque (sin nodo `block`) cuando el `:` ya se consumió.
##
## ## Memoria
## Añade los `stmt` al nodo en construcción.
weave pstmt_parse_block_body_into with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    if not (calling ps_enter_block with p):
        return
    defer calling ps_leave_block with p
    var ignored as int is calling pstmt_parse_block_members with p

## Comprueba la regla de stage0 de “varios statements en una línea”.
##
## Se aplica a los starters duros `var`/`let`/`set`/`const`/`static`.
##
## ## Memoria
## No asigna.
weave pstmt_check_multiple with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    calling ps_skip_error_tokens with p
    if p->pos <= 0:
        return
    var k as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_at with p
    if k != TokKeyword:
        return
    var kw as KeywordKind is calling ps_kw_at with p
    if not (kw == KwVar or kw == KwLet or kw == KwSet or kw == KwConst or kw == KwStatic):
        return
    var cur as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    var prev as Token is p->lex->tokens at (p->pos - 1)
    if (prev.kind == TokDedent) or (prev.kind == TokIndent) or (prev.kind == TokNewline):
        return
    if cur.line != prev.line:
        return
    if prev.kind == TokColon or prev.kind == TokSemicolon:
        return
    if prev.kind == TokKeyword:
        if prev.kw == KwDefer or prev.kw == KwErrdefer or prev.kw == KwStatic:
            return
    calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseMultipleStatements, ""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Statements
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Envuelve en `expr_stmt` un constructo que se usó como expresión.
##
## `if ... then ...` y `for ... then ...` producen `if_expr`/`for_comp`; en
## posición de statement stage0 los envuelve en `expr_stmt`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `expr_stmt` si hace falta.
weave pstmt_wrap_if_expr with p as ref to PsParser, start as int, inner as int into int:
    var k as NodeKind is calling p->ast.kind_of with inner
    if (k == NodeKind.NdIfExpr) or (k == NodeKind.NdForComp) or (k == NodeKind.NdWhenExpr):
        calling ps_begin_children with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, inner
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdExprStmt, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, inner), 0
    return inner

## Parsea un `stmt` completo y lo envuelve en el nodo `stmt`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `stmt`.
weave pstmt_parse_stmt with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var inner as int is calling pstmt_parse_stmt_inner with p
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, inner
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdStmt, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, inner), 0

## Despacha un statement sin envolverlo en `stmt`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye el nodo del statement.
weave pstmt_parse_stmt_inner with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwElse:
        var start_else as int is calling ps_current_start with p
        var ignored_else as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        if calling ps_check with p, TokColon:
            var ignored_colon as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        var off_else as int is calling ps_current_start with p
        calling ps_emit_issue with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseUnexpectedToken, off_else, off_else, "else"
        calling ps_synchronize with p
        return calling ps_error_node with p, start_else, off_else
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwVar:
        return calling pstmt_parse_var with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwLet:
        return calling pstmt_parse_let with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwConst:
        return calling pstmt_parse_const with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwStatic:
        return calling pstmt_parse_static_var with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwSet:
        return calling pstmt_parse_set with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwIf:
        var fn_if as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int is p->hooks.value
        var start_if as int is calling ps_current_start with p
        var inner_if as int is calling fn_if with p
        return calling pstmt_wrap_if_expr with p, start_if, inner_if
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwUnless:
        return calling pstmt_parse_unless with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwWhile:
        return calling pstmt_parse_while with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwFor:
        var fn_for as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int is p->hooks.value
        var start_for as int is calling ps_current_start with p
        var inner_for as int is calling fn_for with p
        return calling pstmt_wrap_if_expr with p, start_for, inner_for
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwWhen:
        var fn_when as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int is p->hooks.when
        var start_when as int is calling ps_current_start with p
        var inner_when as int is calling fn_when with p
        return calling pstmt_wrap_if_expr with p, start_when, inner_when
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwWith:
        if (calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 1) == TokColon:
            var fn_with as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int is p->hooks.with_init
            var start_with as int is calling ps_current_start with p
            var inner_with as int is calling fn_with with p
            calling ps_begin_children with p
            calling ps_add_child with p, inner_with
            return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdExprStmt, start_with, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, inner_with), 0
        return calling pstmt_parse_with_stmt with p
    if calling ps_check_word with p, "unsafe":
        return calling pstmt_parse_unsafe with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwDefer:
        return calling pstmt_parse_defer with p, NodeKind.NdDeferStmt
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwErrdefer:
        return calling pstmt_parse_defer with p, NodeKind.NdErrdeferStmt
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwBanish:
        return calling pstmt_parse_banish with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwReturn:
        return calling pstmt_parse_return with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwBreak:
        return calling pstmt_parse_break_continue with p, NodeKind.NdBreakStmt
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwContinue:
        return calling pstmt_parse_break_continue with p, NodeKind.NdContinueStmt
    if calling ps_check_name_like with p:
        if (calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 1) == TokColon:
            var n2 as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 2
            if n2 == TokKeyword:
                var nkw as KeywordKind is calling ps_kw_at_offset with p, 2
                if nkw == KwFor or nkw == KwWhile:
                    return calling pstmt_parse_labeled_loop with p
    return calling pstmt_parse_expr_stmt with p

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Declaraciones locales
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Parsea un valor de declaración: `indent_literal`, `with:` o `value_expr`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye el nodo del valor.
weave pstmt_parse_decl_value with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    if calling ps_check with p, TokColon:
        return calling patoms.patom_parse_indent_literal with p
    if calling ps_check with p, TokNewline:
        if (calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 1) == TokIndent:
            return calling patoms.patom_parse_indent_literal with p
    return calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_value_expr with p

## Parsea `var NAME [as T] (is value | with:)`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `var_decl`.
weave pstmt_parse_var with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwVar, "'var'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling pstmt_add_name with p, "variable name"
    calling pstmt_add_optional_type with p
    calling pstmt_parse_initializer_into with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdVarDecl, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Parsea `let nombres [as T] (is value | with:)`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `let_decl`.
weave pstmt_parse_let with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwLet, "'let'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    var names as int is calling pstmt_parse_var_names with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, names
    calling pstmt_add_optional_type with p
    calling pstmt_parse_initializer_into with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdLetDecl, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Parsea `const NAME [as T] is value`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `const_decl`.
weave pstmt_parse_const with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwConst, "'const'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling pstmt_add_name with p, "constant name"
    calling pstmt_add_optional_type with p
    var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwIs, "'is'"
    var value as int is calling pstmt_parse_decl_value with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, value
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdConstDecl, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Parsea `static var NAME [as T] (is value | with:)`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `static_var_decl`.
weave pstmt_parse_static_var with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwStatic, "'static'"
    var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwVar, "'var'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling pstmt_add_name with p, "variable name"
    calling pstmt_add_optional_type with p
    calling pstmt_parse_initializer_into with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdStaticVarDecl, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Añade el nombre actual al nodo en construcción.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave pstmt_add_name with p as ref to PsParser, what as string into void:
    calling ps_add_name_like with p

## Añade `as type` o un hijo ausente.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea el nodo de tipo si existe.
weave pstmt_add_optional_type with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwAs:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        var ty as int is calling ptypes.ptype_parse_type with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, ty
    else:
        calling ps_add_absent with p

## Añade el inicializador (`is value` o `with:`) al nodo actual.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye el valor.
weave pstmt_parse_initializer_into with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwIs:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        var value as int is calling pstmt_parse_decl_value with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, value
        return
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwWith:
        if (calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 1) == TokColon:
            var fn as ref to weave with p as ref to PsParser into int is p->hooks.with_init
            var value2 as int is calling fn with p
            calling ps_add_child with p, value2
            return
    calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedToken, "'is'"
    calling ps_add_child with p, (calling ps_error_node with p, (calling ps_current_start with p), (calling ps_current_start with p))

## Parsea la lista de nombres de un `let`.
##
## Acepta `a, b` y `(a, b)`, como la gramática.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `var_name_list`.
weave pstmt_parse_var_names with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    var paren as bool is false
    if calling ps_check with p, TokLeftParen:
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        set paren is true
    var more as bool is true
    while more:
        calling ps_add_name_like with p
        if calling ps_check with p, TokComma:
            var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        else:
            set more is false
    if paren:
        var ignored4 as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokRightParen, "')'"
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdVarNameList, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# set
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Detecta `set xs at n - 1 is v` y emite el diagnóstico específico de stage0.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye y libera el detalle; el bag es dueño del diagnóstico.
weave pstmt_check_at_target with p as ref to PsParser, target as int into void:
    var k as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_at with p
    if not ((k == TokPlus) or (k == TokMinus) or (k == TokStar) or (k == TokSlash) or (k == TokPercent)):
        return
    var n as PsNode is calling p->ast.node_at with target
    if n.child_count == 0:
        return
    var last as int is calling p->ast.child_node_of with target, (n.child_count - 1)
    if last < 0:
        return
    if (calling p->ast.kind_of with last) != NodeKind.NdAtAccess:
        return
    var detail as string is calling pstmt_token_text with p
    defer banish detail
    var off as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_emit_issue with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseAtIndexPrecedence, off, (calling ps_current_end with p), detail
    var more as bool is true
    while more:
        var kk as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_at with p
        if (kk == TokNewline) or (kk == TokDedent) or (kk == TokEof):
            set more is false
        else if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwIs:
            set more is false
        else:
            var skipped as Token is calling ps_advance with p

## Texto del token actual.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
weave pstmt_token_text with p as ref to PsParser into string:
    var t as Token is calling ps_current_token with p
    var sp as pspan.ByteSpan is calling pstoken.token_span with t
    return calling p->src.slice with sp

## Parsea `set target is value` o `set target OP value`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea `set_stmt` o `compound_set_stmt`.
weave pstmt_parse_set with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwSet, "'set'"
    var raw_target as int is calling pstmt_parse_set_target with p
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, raw_target
    var target as int is calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdSetTarget, (calling pexpr.pexpr_start_of with p, raw_target), (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, raw_target), 0
    calling pstmt_check_at_target with p, raw_target
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwIs:
        var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        calling ps_begin_children with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, target
        var value as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_value_expr with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, value
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdSetStmt, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, value), 0
    var opk as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_at with p
    if (opk == TokPlusAssign) or (opk == TokMinusAssign) or (opk == TokStarAssign) or (opk == TokSlashAssign) or (opk == TokPercentAssign) or (opk == TokAmpersandAssign) or (opk == TokVerticalBarAssign) or (opk == TokCaretAssign) or (opk == TokShiftLeftAssign) or (opk == TokShiftRightAssign):
        var opi as int is p->pos
        var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        calling ps_begin_children with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, target
        calling ps_add_token with p, opi
        var value2 as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, value2
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdCompoundSetStmt, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, value2), opi
    calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedToken, "'is'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, target
    calling ps_add_child with p, (calling ps_error_node with p, (calling ps_current_start with p), (calling ps_current_start with p))
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdSetStmt, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Parsea el target de un `set`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea `with_target`, `normal_target` o `essence_target`.
weave pstmt_parse_set_target with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    if calling ps_check with p, TokDot:
        return calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_with_target with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwEssence:
        var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
        var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwOf, "'of'"
        calling ps_begin_children with p
        var inner as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_unary with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, inner
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdEssenceTarget, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, inner), 0
    return calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_normal_target with p

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Control de flujo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Parsea la condición de un `if`, incluyendo la forma de binding.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea `if_cond` o `if_cond_binding`.
weave pstmt_parse_if_cond with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    if calling ps_check_name_like with p:
        if (calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 1) == TokKeyword:
            if (calling ps_kw_at_offset with p, 1) == KwAs:
                calling ps_begin_children with p
                calling ps_add_name_like with p
                var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwAs, "'as'"
                var ty as int is calling ptypes.ptype_parse_type with p
                calling ps_add_child with p, ty
                var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwIs, "'is'"
                var value as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
                calling ps_add_child with p, value
                return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdIfCondBinding, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, value), 0
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    var cond as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, cond
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdIfCond, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, cond), 0

## Parsea un `if` completo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `if_stmt`.
weave pstmt_parse_if with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwIf, "'if'"
    var cond as int is calling pstmt_parse_if_cond with p
    return calling pstmt_parse_if_tail with p, start, cond

## Termina un `if` después de la condición.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea `if_stmt` y opcionalmente `else_block`.
weave pstmt_parse_if_tail with p as ref to PsParser, start as int, cond as int into int:
    var block as int is calling pstmt_parse_block with p
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, cond
    calling ps_add_child with p, block
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwElse:
        var eb as int is calling pstmt_parse_else_block with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, eb
    else:
        calling ps_add_absent with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdIfStmt, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Parsea `else ...`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `else_block`.
weave pstmt_parse_else_block with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwElse, "'else'"
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwIf:
        calling ps_begin_children with p
        var nested as int is calling pstmt_parse_if with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, nested
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdElseBlock, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, nested), 0
    var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokColon, "':'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    if calling ps_check with p, TokNewline:
        var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        var ignored4 as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokIndent, "indent"
        var more as bool is true
        while more:
            calling ps_skip_newlines with p
            if (calling ps_check with p, TokDedent) or (calling ps_check with p, TokEof):
                set more is false
            else:
                var before as int is p->pos
                var st as int is calling pstmt_parse_stmt with p
                calling ps_add_child with p, st
                calling pstmt_check_multiple with p
                if p->pos == before:
                    var forced as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        if calling ps_check with p, TokDedent:
            var ignored5 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        else:
            calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedDedent, ""
    else:
        var simple as int is calling pstmt_parse_simple_stmt with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, simple
        calling ps_finish_statement with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdElseBlock, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Parsea un `unless`.
